cff-version: 1.2.0
# Software citation for the curated Sentinel-2/EuroCrops crop-segmentation
# package. The DOI identifies a RESERVED Zenodo new-version draft;
# it is not evidence that the record is already published.
# date-released is only asserted if the author supplies the intended
# publication date at preparation time.
# `preferred-citation` IS present, and carries `status: submitted` with no DOI.
# The manuscript is under review: it is neither accepted nor published, and
# nothing here may suggest otherwise. The status is what makes the reference
# honest, so the checker requires a DOI-less preferred-citation to declare one.
message: "Cite this software when using the Sentinel-2/EuroCrops crop-segmentation pipeline. This record describes the SOFTWARE only; prefer the associated manuscript, which is currently under review and carries no DOI. The dataset and model weights are separate Zenodo records; see release/ZENODO_DEPOSIT_ARCHITECTURE.md."
type: software
title: "Sentinel-2 Crop Segmentation: Curated Research Software"
abstract: >-
  Research software for building and evaluating a Sentinel-2 Level-2A
  semantic-segmentation benchmark over EuroCrops parcel annotations. It
  covers Sentinel-2 scene discovery and SAFE loading, Scene Classification
  Layer cloud and nodata filtering, grid and hotcell region-of-interest
  selection, ten-band 256x256 patch and mask generation, patch-level
  provenance logging, geographically blocked train/validation/test splitting
  and out-of-fold planning, optional crop-calendar scene-acquisition windows,
  four-level U-Net training, checkpoint evaluation and prediction, and a
  post-training label-uncertainty review filter that consumes precomputed
  parcel-review evidence. The package distributes code, configuration and
  tests only: Sentinel-2 products, EuroCrops vectors, the article dataset and
  trained weights are obtained or cited separately.
authors:
  - family-names: "Scarlat"
    given-names: "Alexandra Nicoleta"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-5924-3027"
    affiliation: "Transilvania University of Brașov, Faculty of Mathematics and Computer Science"
version: "2.0.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23714448"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/AlexandraScarlat15/sentinel-crop-seg"
keywords:
  - Sentinel-2
  - EuroCrops
  - crop mapping
  - semantic segmentation
  - remote sensing
  - reproducibility
# The work this software supports. Authorship here is the MANUSCRIPT's author
# list and is deliberately not the same as the software `authors` above: this
# record credits who wrote the code, the citation below credits who wrote the
# paper.
